{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778195508,"nonce":"WDk8vYmR59Bf9/baKP1NEZEK63Q=","title":"cleanup_merged_worktrees uses wrong relative path to dwt — silently skips all cleanup","message":"## Bug\n\n`cleanup_merged_worktrees()` in `cli/auth-merge.sh` (lines 325-350) resolves `dwt` via a relative path:\n\n```bash\nscript_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" \u0026\u0026 pwd)\"\nlocal dwt=\"${script_dir}/../../../../bin/dwt\"\ndwt=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$dwt\")\" \u0026\u0026 pwd)/$(basename \"$dwt\")\"\n```\n\nThe comment says \"dwt is in bin/ which is `../../../../bin/` relative to cli/\". This is wrong.\n\n`auth-merge.sh` lives at `/Users/mll/Main/10 Projects/05 Utils/mandible/cli/auth-merge.sh`.\nFour levels up from `cli/` resolves to `/Users/mll/Main/`, not `~/.dotfiles/`.\nThe computed path is `/Users/mll/Main/bin/dwt` which does not exist.\n\nThe guard `[[ -x \"$dwt\" ]] || return 0` then silently exits without cleaning up anything.\n\n## Impact\n\nEvery auth merge since this code was written (initial commit `5ed6c33`) has silently skipped worktree cleanup. Three confirmed stale worktrees post the bash-portability fix (commit `39e2978` in dotfiles, auth `a8c3a63e`):\n\n- `feature/induced-gain-first-run` (rlrmp, auth `cab29866`)\n- `feature/feedbax-graph-step-adapter` (rlrmp, auth `99bb7f1c`)\n- `feature/graph-public-step` (feedbax, auth `5456e5be`)\n\n## Fix\n\nReplace the fragile relative path with a `command -v dwt` lookup. The fallback `~/.local/bin/dwt` symlink already exists and is always on PATH.\n\n```bash\ncleanup_merged_worktrees() {\n  local branch=\"$1\"\n  local dwt\n  dwt=\"$(command -v dwt 2\u003e/dev/null)\" || {\n    # fallback to known symlink location\n    [[ -x \"${HOME}/.local/bin/dwt\" ]] \u0026\u0026 dwt=\"${HOME}/.local/bin/dwt\"\n  }\n  [[ -n \"$dwt\" \u0026\u0026 -x \"$dwt\" ]] || return 0\n  # ... rest unchanged\n}\n```\n\n## Note\n\nThe bash-portability fix to `dwt` (dotfiles commit `39e2978`) was a necessary prerequisite (dwt was zsh-only and auth-merge.sh runs under bash), but the path-resolution bug existed independently and was never addressed.","files":null}]}